cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use NullCity in academic work, a benchmark comparison, or a
  derivative tool, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "NullCity: A Deterministic, Partially Observable Crisis-Decision Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  NullCity is an open-source, local-first crisis decision benchmark with
  deterministic replay, strict truth/belief information boundaries,
  human/agent interface parity, and verifiable (tamper-evident) run
  artifacts. Players and agents act on delayed, incomplete, and sometimes
  false reports rather than ground-truth state; every completed run can be
  replayed, compared, and independently re-verified from its public event
  log.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-07"
license: MIT
